ortly sanctions  on a substantial number of individuals  responsible for violence  repression and election throat  we call on the belarusian authorities to  find a peaceful way out of the crisis  by ending by ending the violence  distillating tensions  and launching an inclusive national  dialogue  all parties including third states  should support such a process we will  continue to follow the situation closely  and stand ready to contribute to efforts  to peacefully end the crisis the eu  fully supports osce proposals for  dialogue in belarus  and is ready to provide assistance  to further them to conclude  i would like to address the people of  belarus directly  we stand by your side in your desire to  exercise your fundamental  democratic rights and in your desire for  a peaceful  democratic and prosperous future  we had also the occasion to raise the  situation  in the eastern mediterranean and  this question and relations with turkey  were raised by different member states  we expressed our full solidarity with  greece and cell priests  and we called and reaffirmed our  previous conclusions  on the illegal drilling activities  we agreed to revert on to those issues  during our meeting in september all  options will be on the table  finally we raised  the event in mali the events in mali are  of deep concern  and can have a destabilizing impact on  the entire region  and on the fight against terrorism  thank you mr president we will now turn  to the president of the european  commission  madam president thank you  but uh thank you shao  the people of belarus want change  and they want it now and  we are impressed by the courage  of the people of belarus for exactly 10  days  since the presidential election took  place  the people of belarus have taken to the  streets  in unprecedented numbers  they demand the release of all  unlawfully detained  prisoners the prosecution of those  responsible for police brutality  they want freedom of speech and assembly  and t