tin it was the occasion for  me  to express a very strong european  conviction  we are convinced indeed that it's  important to give the possibility  in belarus through a national dialogue  to find a solution  and indeed i repeat that we want to  avoid  external negative interferences and yet  the occasion we sir  when you put into a very clear and very  friendly exchange of views  and change of opinions about the current  situation  and probably you have observed uh  the last hours uh some statements made  by the kremlin  uh in in the direction that they don't  intend in those current circumstances  uh to intervene in belarus at the  military level  turning to the president of the european  commission  madam president yes  thank you baron it is the belarusian  people  who are demanding a re-run of  truly free and fair elections and i want  to be very clear  and this is is the attitude  we have that we support the belarusian  people  in them choosing the path they  want to have they want to go down  so it's their decision on where they  want to  um lead their country to too  but we support them but we have the  respect  that the belarusian people themselves  are free to decide and  to determine how they want to shape  their country  and how they see the future of belarus  now we're going to take two more  questions uh first of all jakobo  barigatsi from politico jacopo can you  hear us  is can you hear me yes please hey i  have uh thank you thank you byron i have  a couple of questions for  president michelle first of all during  your contacts you reach out also  to our transatlantic partners uh to  coordinate any kind of  effort and secondly uh what do you think  that uh we'll avoid uh a repetition of  the situation that we had  in ukraine uh with the russian  annexation of  crimea and so on uh whether we have  whether the you has  learned from uh what happened there  uh to avoid repetition of these things  european  [Music]  situation  [Music]  last question now f